An :IF opened at script level does not contain an :ELSE inside a
procedure: the owning-block search stops at the enclosing :PROCEDURE,
because a procedure compiles on its own. The :ELSE is stray even though an
:IF is open further out (diag.stray_block_keyword, fourth Flags fence).
-- input.ssl --
:DECLARE bVerbose;
bVerbose := .T.;
:IF bVerbose;
:PROCEDURE LogLine;
	:PARAMETERS sText;
:ELSE;
	sText := "";
:ENDPROC;
:ENDIF;
-- format --
:DECLARE bVerbose;

bVerbose := .T.;

:IF bVerbose;
	:PROCEDURE LogLine;
		:PARAMETERS sText;
	:ELSE;
		sText := "";
	:ENDPROC;
:ENDIF;
-- diagnostics --
6:1-6:6 error stray_block_keyword: ':ELSE' is outside any ':IF' block
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
6:1-6:6 error stray_block_keyword: ':ELSE' is outside any ':IF' block
